From e2e8bef570bbe5882a66375ed241eda2fdc1a411 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom J Nowell <contact@tomjn.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 17:20:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] zink: release command pool resources on reset

Origin:      ours
Status:      candidate
Applies-to:  mesa 56588ef0665ab81fa16248489542c1747fdf99ef
Expires:     when proposed upstream and merged, or when KosmicKrisp stops
             retaining allocator memory across a pool reset
Evidence:    engine peak 12288 MiB -> 7049 MiB over a 120s run, combined with
             MR 43697. No effect on its own. Reproducer unchanged at 474mb,
             which is expected: it resets the pool about once.
             coding-agents/MACOS_PERFORMANCE.md, "Mesa pin and issue 15998"

Zink resets its command pools with flags = 0, which permits an
implementation to retain the memory for reuse. Every driver Zink runs on
pools that memory and hands it to the next recording, so this is normally
the right default.

KosmicKrisp retains it per MTL4CommandAllocator instead, where nothing
else can reach it, and an allocator only returns memory to the system when
it is destroyed. The result is growth that never plateaus under a steady
workload, because Zink never asks for the memory back.

Passing VK_COMMAND_POOL_RESET_RELEASE_RESOURCES_BIT asks for it. On its
own this changes nothing, because KosmicKrisp declares the flag UNUSED in
kk_reset_cmd_buffer and has no kk_ResetCommandPool at all. Combined with
MR 43697, which adds one that honours the bit, engine peak footprint on a
120s run falls from 12288 MiB to 7049 MiB.

Not proposed upstream yet: this changes behaviour for every driver Zink
targets, and the cost to drivers that already reuse the memory well has
not been measured.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c
index e7cdc69a920..1a38fef228e 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_batch.c
@@ -56,10 +56,10 @@ static void
 reset_batch_state_internal(struct zink_screen *screen, struct zink_batch_state *bs)
 {
    MESA_TRACE_FUNC();
-   VkResult result = VKSCR(ResetCommandPool)(screen->dev, bs->cmdpool, 0);
+   VkResult result = VKSCR(ResetCommandPool)(screen->dev, bs->cmdpool, VK_COMMAND_POOL_RESET_RELEASE_RESOURCES_BIT);
    if (result != VK_SUCCESS)
       mesa_loge("ZINK: vkResetCommandPool failed (%s)", vk_Result_to_str(result));
-   result = VKSCR(ResetCommandPool)(screen->dev, bs->unsynchronized_cmdpool, 0);
+   result = VKSCR(ResetCommandPool)(screen->dev, bs->unsynchronized_cmdpool, VK_COMMAND_POOL_RESET_RELEASE_RESOURCES_BIT);
    if (result != VK_SUCCESS)
       mesa_loge("ZINK: vkResetCommandPool failed (%s)", vk_Result_to_str(result));
 
